# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working data. None of this belongs in the repository, and LEGAL.md and the
# README both say so — but .gitignore does not apply to files already tracked,
# and these were. Use `git rm --cached` once; the patterns keep them out after.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The application database. It holds extracted claims and quotations from
# full-text papers, which are the publishers' content and not redistributable,
# and it changes on every run — so it also makes every commit a binary diff.
aop_rag.db
aop_rag.backup-*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Replicate-measurement output from tools/replicate_run.py.
replicates.db

# Uploaded or staged full-text papers.
papers/
example_files/*.pdf

# API keys, if anyone ever writes them to a file rather than the sidebar.
.env
*.key

# AOP-Wiki XML dump. This is AOP-Wiki's curated database, not ours, and
# redistributing ~10 MB of it inside a code repository is a licensing decision
# rather than a packaging one. The application downloads it on request instead
# (sidebar → AOP-Wiki dump), and runs without it if it is absent.
stage2_extraction/aopwiki_data/*.gz

# Corpus manifests. A CSV of DOIs, titles and publishers identifies the exact
# articles processed; the tool ships without one.
licences.csv
licenses.csv
corpus.csv
dois.csv

# Staging area for files pending manual deletion.
_to_delete/
